---
source: crates/construct-dev/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "shaped(&env, &req)"
---
{
  "bytes": 5464,
  "n_tools": 9,
  "request": {
    "model": "openrouter/free",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "system",
        "content": "You are construct, a coding agent working in the user's terminal. Use your tools to do what the user asks, then stop.\n\n- Read before you edit. Make the smallest change that does the job and match the surrounding code.\n- Prefer read/grep/glob/edit over shell for files. Run independent tool calls in parallel.\n- Verify your work (build, test, run) when you can, and report failures honestly.\n- Be brief. Use GitHub markdown. Refer to code as path:line.\n- Don't narrate before tool calls. When done, say what changed and how you verified it in a few sentences.\n- The skill library is outside the workspace; read and change skills only with the skill and skill_manage tools, never file tools or shell.\n- Tools see only the workspace, system paths and toolchains. Search the workspace, not the whole filesystem; if something isn't there, ask the user where it is.\n- <system-reminder> blocks come from the harness, not the user.\n\n# Environment\n- cwd: [WORK]\n- os: [OS]\n- date: [DATE]\n"
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "what did we decide about the parser last time?"
      }
    ],
    "stream": true,
    "stream_options": {
      "include_usage": true
    },
    "tools": [
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "shell",
          "description": "Run a bash command and return its combined stdout/stderr. Use for builds, tests, git, and anything without a dedicated tool. Default timeout 120s.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "command": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "workdir": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Directory to run in; defaults to the session's"
              },
              "timeout": {
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "Seconds, max 1800"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "command"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "read",
          "description": "Read a text file with line numbers (or list a directory). Reads up to 2000 lines; use offset/limit for more.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "path": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "offset": {
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "1-based first line"
              },
              "limit": {
                "type": "integer"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "path"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "write",
          "description": "Create a file or replace its whole content. An existing file must be read first. Prefer edit for changes.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "path": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "path",
              "content"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "edit",
          "description": "Replace exact text in a file. old_string must match once (copy it from read output without the line-number prefix) unless replace_all is set. Tolerates quote/dash and trailing-whitespace differences.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "path": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "old_string": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "new_string": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "replace_all": {
                "type": "boolean"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "path",
              "old_string",
              "new_string"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "grep",
          "description": "Search file contents with a regex (ripgrep engine, respects .gitignore). Returns path:line: text.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "pattern": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "path": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "File or directory; defaults to the session's"
              },
              "include": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Glob filter, e.g. *.rs"
              },
              "ignore_case": {
                "type": "boolean"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "pattern"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "glob",
          "description": "Find files by glob pattern (e.g. src/**/*.rs), newest first. Respects .gitignore.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "pattern": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "path": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "pattern"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "recall_result",
          "description": "Return the full original output of an earlier tool call in this project, by its call id. Use when an earlier result was cut, summarized or is no longer in view.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The tool call id"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "id"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "journal_query",
          "description": "Read-only SQLite over this project's journal: every past session's messages and tool calls. One SELECT (or WITH) statement; at most 200 rows / 16 KB come back, and a query is stopped after 5 s.\nTable events(seq INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, session_id TEXT, type TEXT, v INT, at_ms INT unix ms, payload TEXT JSON).\ntype and its payload fields: head (cwd, model; a session's first row), user / assistant (message.content; assistant also message.tool_calls), tool_start (id, name, args), tool_end (id, name, ok, ms, code, output), tool_result (id, message.content), route (groups, skills), request, usage, turn_start, turn_end, compacted, error.\nRead a field with json_extract(payload, '$.name'), e.g. WHERE type = 'tool_end' AND json_extract(payload, '$.ok') = 0.\nKeyword search over user, assistant and tool_result text: SELECT e.session_id, e.type, snippet(events_fts, 0, '[', ']', '…', 12) FROM events_fts JOIN events e ON e.seq = events_fts.rowid WHERE events_fts MATCH 'word' ORDER BY rank LIMIT 20.",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "sql": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "sql"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
          "name": "enable_tools",
          "description": "Switch on more tools for this session when you need them: web (web_search, web_fetch); memory (durable memory of the user and machine); skills (load saved procedures); skill-write (write the skill library).",
          "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "groups": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "web",
                    "memory",
                    "skills",
                    "skill-write"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "groups"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
